WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:01.715
Module 6.

00:02.065 --> 00:04.352
Confidentiality and data handling.

00:04.702 --> 00:08.641
This module sets out practical rules for protecting client confidentiality

00:08.641 --> 00:12.580
and privilege when using AI tools, including how to read

00:12.580 --> 00:16.126
vendor data terms and when client consent is required.

00:17.876 --> 00:22.984
By the end of this module you will be able to: classify information

00:22.984 --> 00:28.093
before it goes into any AI tool; distinguish enterprise and consumer data terms;

00:28.093 --> 00:33.201
apply anonymisation and minimisation techniques; know when to stop and get client consent.

00:34.951 --> 00:38.141
Before any client information goes into an AI tool, someone

00:38.141 --> 00:41.011
at the firm must know the tool's data terms.

00:41.361 --> 00:43.080
Ask six questions.

00:43.430 --> 00:45.995
Is this an enterprise or a consumer plan?

00:46.345 --> 00:50.757
Consumer plans often have weaker confidentiality and retention terms.

00:51.107 --> 00:53.789
Are inputs used to train the vendor's models?

00:54.139 --> 00:57.390
If so, client data could surface in later outputs.

00:57.740 --> 01:00.097
How long are inputs and outputs kept?

01:00.447 --> 01:04.092
Who at the vendor can access the data, including for human review?

01:04.442 --> 01:07.290
Where is data stored and processed, since some

01:07.290 --> 01:09.783
clients and some matters restrict data location?

01:10.133 --> 01:12.616
And can logs be exported, because you may

01:12.616 --> 01:14.788
need them to prove what happened later.

01:16.538 --> 01:18.698
Use simple traffic-light rules.

01:19.048 --> 01:23.059
Green is public or fully anonymised material: published law,

01:23.059 --> 01:27.070
public filings, and text with all identifying details removed.

01:27.420 --> 01:29.731
It can go into any approved tool.

01:30.081 --> 01:35.653
Amber is client confidential information: client facts, contracts and correspondence.

01:36.003 --> 01:39.767
It goes only into firm-approved enterprise tools with confirmed no-training

01:39.767 --> 01:43.155
terms, and only as much as the task needs.

01:43.505 --> 01:48.525
Red is material that never goes into an AI tool without specific approval:

01:48.525 --> 01:53.546
privileged strategy, health and financial records, sealed or protected material, data under a

01:53.546 --> 01:58.180
protective order, and anything a client has told you not to share.

01:58.530 --> 02:02.228
Red material needs approval from the firm's AI Governance

02:02.228 --> 02:05.926
Lead and, for self-learning tools, the client's informed consent.

02:07.676 --> 02:10.090
Two habits reduce risk dramatically.

02:10.440 --> 02:12.333
Minimise and anonymise.

02:12.683 --> 02:16.982
Replace identifiers with neutral labels such as Client A, Company B

02:16.982 --> 02:20.891
or the Property, instead of names, addresses and account numbers.

02:21.241 --> 02:23.984
Send only what the task needs: paste the

02:23.984 --> 02:26.384
relevant clause, not the whole data room.

02:26.734 --> 02:28.464
And check what you upload.

02:28.814 --> 02:32.053
Metadata, tracked changes and hidden comments travel with documents,

02:32.053 --> 02:35.293
and they can reveal more than the visible text.

02:37.042 --> 02:38.401
One insurance note.

02:38.751 --> 02:43.430
This training reduces both the chance and the size of a confidentiality incident.

02:43.780 --> 02:47.696
But data and privacy incidents, including those caused by putting

02:47.696 --> 02:51.613
client information into an AI tool, are often handled under

02:51.613 --> 02:55.529
cyber or privacy insurance rather than under professional liability insurance.

02:55.879 --> 03:00.660
Confirm with your broker which of your policies responds to an AI-related data

03:00.660 --> 03:05.074
incident, and make sure your incident process notifies the right insurer quickly.

03:06.824 --> 03:08.519
Let's recap the key points.

03:08.869 --> 03:11.644
Know each tool's data terms before use.

03:11.994 --> 03:15.546
Green, amber, red: classify before you paste.

03:15.896 --> 03:18.195
Minimise and anonymise by default.

03:18.545 --> 03:22.806
Self-learning tools plus confidential data means informed client consent.

03:24.556 --> 03:25.647
Knowledge check.

03:25.997 --> 03:29.817
An associate wants to paste a full merger agreement under a

03:29.817 --> 03:33.637
confidentiality agreement into a free consumer chatbot to get a summary.

03:33.987 --> 03:35.833
What is the right response?

03:36.183 --> 03:39.364
Option A: Fine if they delete the chat afterwards.

03:39.714 --> 03:43.980
Option B: Not permitted: this is amber or red data

03:43.980 --> 03:48.247
and needs an approved enterprise tool, minimisation and possibly consent.

03:48.597 --> 03:52.301
Option C: Fine if they remove the company names only.

03:52.651 --> 03:55.333
Take a moment to decide before the answer appears.

04:01.082 --> 04:02.615
The answer is option B.

04:02.965 --> 04:05.949
Consumer tools may retain or train on inputs.

04:06.299 --> 04:12.765
Confidential material goes only into approved tools, minimised, with approval and consent where required.
